{"type":"text","timestamp":1792510204706,"sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","part":{"id":"prt_159ef02ba001ZpuEDNXdZ1j18Y","messageID":"msg_159ed45590019gV2oFTws2guE1","sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","type":"text","text":"\n\nThe pack `dynamic_bfs` is a calibration problem: maintain a BFS tree from root 0 under edge flips. `work_ratio` is the wall-time ratio against a full BFS recompute. My plan:\n\n- **Insert (u,v)**: only matters if `dist[u]+1 < dist[v]` (or v unreachable). Re-attach v under u, then propagate the decrease with a BFS that relaxes only shortening edges.\n- **Delete (u,v)**: if not a tree edge, no-op (the tree still certifies all distances). Otherwise re-attach the subtree under v in BFS order (a vertex keeps its distance iff it has a surviving in-neighbor one level up), then Dijkstra the lost remainder from the surviving boundary.\n\nWriting the candidate:\n\n","time":{"start":1792510198458,"end":1792510204697}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792510204730,"sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-904c58bc40b0e625","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s3/candidate.py","content":"\"\"\"Dynamic BFS tree from a fixed root (vertex 0) in a directed graph.\n\nInsertion of (u, v) can only shorten distances, and only when\ndist[u] + 1 < dist[v] (or v was unreachable): re-attach v under u and\npropagate the decrease with a BFS that relaxes only shortening edges.\nDeletion of a non-tree edge changes nothing (the tree still certifies\nevery distance). Deletion of the tree edge (u, v) re-attaches the\nsubtree under v in BFS order -- a vertex keeps its distance iff it has\na surviving in-neighbor one level up -- and re-reaches the lost\nremainder from the surviving boundary with a Dijkstra pass.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport heapq\n\n\ndef _init_bfs(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    parent = [None] * n\n    dist = [-1] * n\n    dist[0] = 0\n    queue = [0]\n    for u in queue:\n        row = graph[u]\n        nd = dist[u] + 1\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v] and dist[v] == -1:\n                dist[v] = nd\n                parent[v] = u\n                queue.append(v)\n    return parent, dist\n\n\ndef _rebuild_children(parent):\n    children = [[] for _ in parent]\n    for v, p in enumerate(parent):\n        if p is not None:\n            children[p].append(v)\n    return children\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    parent, dist = _init_bfs(graph)\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"distances\": dist,\n            \"children\": _rebuild_children(parent)}\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    dist = state[\"distances\"]\n    if dist[u] == -1 or (dist[v] != -1 and dist[u] + 1 >= dist[v]):\n        return state\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    children = state[\"children\"]\n    old = parent[v]\n    if old is not None:\n        children[old].remove(v)\n    parent[v] = u\n    dist[v] = dist[u] + 1\n    children[u].append(v)\n    n = len(graph)\n    queue = [v]\n    for x in queue:\n        row = graph[x]\n        nd = dist[x] + 1\n        for y in range(n):\n            if not row[y]:\n                continue\n            dy = dist[y]\n            if dy == -1:\n                dist[y] = nd\n                parent[y] = x\n                children[x].append(y)\n                queue.append(y)\n            elif dy > nd:\n                children[parent[y]].remove(y)\n                parent[y] = x\n                dist[y] = nd\n                children[x].append(y)\n                queue.append(y)\n    return state\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    if parent[v] != u:\n        return state\n    dist = state[\"distances\"]\n    n = len(graph)\n    # Subtree under v in BFS order (non-decreasing distance).\n    subtree = []\n    queue = [v]\n    for x in queue:\n        subtree.append(x)\n        queue.extend(state[\"children\"][x])\n    lost = set()\n    # Phase 1: in BFS order, a vertex keeps its distance iff it has a\n    # surviving in-neighbor exactly one level up.\n    for x in subtree:\n        kept = False\n        for z in range(n):\n            if graph[z][x] and dist[z] + 1 == dist[x] and z not in lost:\n                parent[x] = z\n                kept = True\n                break\n        if not kept:\n            lost.add(x)\n            dist[x] = -1\n            parent[x] = None\n    # Phase 2: lost vertices may still be reachable at a larger distance.\n    if lost:\n        best = {}\n        par2 = {}\n        heap = []\n        for x in lost:\n            bd = None\n            bz = None\n            for z in range(n):\n                if graph[z][x] and z not in lost:\n                    d = dist[z] + 1\n                    if bd is None or d < bd:\n                        bd = d\n                        bz = z\n            if bd is not None:\n                best[x] = bd\n                par2[x] = bz\n                heap.append((bd, x))\n        heapq.heapify(heap)\n        while heap:\n            d, x = heapq.heappop(heap)\n            if d != best.get(x):\n                continue\n            row = graph[x]\n            nd = d + 1\n            for y in range(n):\n                if row[y] and y in lost and (y not in best or nd < best[y]):\n                    best[y] = nd\n                    par2[y] = x\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, (nd, y))\n        for x in lost:\n            if x in best:\n                dist[x] = best[x]\n                parent[x] = par2[x]\n    state[\"children\"] = _rebuild_children(parent)\n    return state\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s3/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s3/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792510204684,"end":1792510204722}},"id":"prt_159ef0625001sfIFqCHWJJ9Smk","sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","messageID":"msg_159ed45590019gV2oFTws2guE1"}}
