{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1792510512676,"sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","part":{"id":"prt_159f3cdf4001xvzy0tmzysjlbT","messageID":"msg_159f3ca6b001X2S3LSe1lfZIga","sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","snapshot":"184e16a9242ed79ef93cde936b954d854a85ea16","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1792510543311,"sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","part":{"id":"prt_159f403af001Os8DI127eAUWZy","messageID":"msg_159f3ca6b001X2S3LSe1lfZIga","sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","type":"text","text":"\n\nI found that the delete operation is the main performance bottleneck at 1241ns per call, with column scans being the culprit. I'll fix this by maintaining a transposed matrix in the state so that phase 1/2 can do row scans instead, and I've also identified that the `z not in lost` checks are redundant since lost vertices already have `dist == -1`.\n\n","time":{"start":1792510526383,"end":1792510543303}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792510543343,"sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a2e61f713f19bc60","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s3/candidate.py","content":"\"\"\"Dynamic BFS tree from a fixed root (vertex 0) in a directed graph.\n\nInsertion of (u, v) can only shorten distances, and only when\ndist[u] + 1 < dist[v] (or v was unreachable): re-attach v under u and\npropagate the decrease with a BFS that relaxes only shortening edges.\nDeletion of a non-tree edge changes nothing (the tree still certifies\nevery distance). Deletion of the tree edge (u, v) re-attaches the\nsubtree under v in BFS order -- a vertex keeps its distance iff it has\na surviving in-neighbor one level up -- and re-reaches the lost\nremainder from the surviving boundary with a Dijkstra pass.\n\nThe state keeps a transposed adjacency matrix so in-neighborhoods are\nrow scans; it is maintained in O(1) per update.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport heapq\n\n\ndef _init_bfs(graph):\n    n = len(graph)\n    parent = [None] * n\n    dist = [-1] * n\n    dist[0] = 0\n    queue = [0]\n    for u in queue:\n        row = graph[u]\n        nd = dist[u] + 1\n        for v in range(n):\n            if row[v] and dist[v] == -1:\n                dist[v] = nd\n                parent[v] = u\n                queue.append(v)\n    return parent, dist\n\n\ndef _rebuild_children(parent):\n    children = [[] for _ in parent]\n    for v, p in enumerate(parent):\n        if p is not None:\n            children[p].append(v)\n    return children\n\n\ndef init(graph):\n    parent, dist = _init_bfs(graph)\n    inn = [list(row) for row in zip(*graph)]\n    return {\"parent\": parent, \"distances\": dist,\n            \"children\": _rebuild_children(parent), \"inn\": inn}\n\n\ndef insert_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    dist = state[\"distances\"]\n    state[\"inn\"][v][u] = 1\n    if dist[u] == -1 or (dist[v] != -1 and dist[u] + 1 >= dist[v]):\n        return state\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    children = state[\"children\"]\n    old = parent[v]\n    if old is not None:\n        children[old].remove(v)\n    parent[v] = u\n    dist[v] = dist[u] + 1\n    children[u].append(v)\n    n = len(graph)\n    queue = [v]\n    for x in queue:\n        row = graph[x]\n        nd = dist[x] + 1\n        for y in range(n):\n            if not row[y]:\n                continue\n            dy = dist[y]\n            if dy == -1:\n                dist[y] = nd\n                parent[y] = x\n                children[x].append(y)\n                queue.append(y)\n            elif dy > nd:\n                children[parent[y]].remove(y)\n                parent[y] = x\n                dist[y] = nd\n                children[x].append(y)\n                queue.append(y)\n    return state\n\n\ndef delete_edge(graph, edge, state):\n    u, v = edge\n    parent = state[\"parent\"]\n    state[\"inn\"][v][u] = 0\n    if parent[v] != u:\n        return state\n    dist = state[\"distances\"]\n    n = len(graph)\n    inn = state[\"inn\"]\n    # Subtree under v in BFS order (non-decreasing distance).\n    subtree = []\n    queue = [v]\n    for x in queue:\n        subtree.append(x)\n        queue.extend(state[\"children\"][x])\n    lost = set()\n    # Phase 1: in BFS order, a vertex keeps its distance iff it has a\n    # surviving in-neighbor exactly one level up. Lost vertices carry\n    # dist -1, so the level test alone excludes them.\n    for x in subtree:\n        dx = dist[x]\n        row = inn[x]\n        kept = False\n        for z in range(n):\n            if row[z] and dist[z] + 1 == dx:\n                parent[x] = z\n                kept = True\n                break\n        if not kept:\n            lost.add(x)\n            dist[x] = -1\n            parent[x] = None\n    # Phase 2: lost vertices may still be reachable at a larger distance.\n    if lost:\n        best = {}\n        par2 = {}\n        heap = []\n        for x in lost:\n            bd = None\n            bz = None\n            row = inn[x]\n            for z in range(n):\n                if row[z] and dist[z] != -1:\n                    d = dist[z] + 1\n                    if bd is None or d < bd:\n                        bd = d\n                        bz = z\n            if bd is not None:\n                best[x] = bd\n                par2[x] = bz\n                heap.append((bd, x))\n        heapq.heapify(heap)\n        while heap:\n            d, x = heapq.heappop(heap)\n            if d != best.get(x):\n                continue\n            row = graph[x]\n            nd = d + 1\n            for y in range(n):\n                if row[y] and y in lost and (y not in best or nd < best[y]):\n                    best[y] = nd\n                    par2[y] = x\n                    heapq.heappush(heap, (nd, y))\n        for x in lost:\n            if x in best:\n                dist[x] = best[x]\n                parent[x] = par2[x]\n    state[\"children\"] = _rebuild_children(parent)\n    return state\n"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/ethomdt/thesis/runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s3/candidate.py","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"runs/eval1_harness_dynamic_bfs_s3/candidate.py","time":{"start":1792510543293,"end":1792510543337}},"id":"prt_159f406a9001XHCe0r0lsUdFo9","sessionID":"ses_ea6165c0bffec0GbYC1A6HUELg","messageID":"msg_159f3ca6b001X2S3LSe1lfZIga"}}
